\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Analyzed negative-mass Schwarzschild visibility and proved its initial slice is incomplete, rejecting it as a counterexample to the source regular-data conjecture.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and reference entries for 30004804. The historical source/context and inherited status are retained; no fresh literature or novelty certification is claimed. No external theorem is used without proof in this attempt; explicit model assumptions are distinguished from facts about the source model.

\paragraph{Rejecting a tempting naked-singularity counterexample.} Put \(M=-a\), \(a>0\), in the Schwarzschild form, so \(f(r)=1+2a/r>0\) for every \(r>0\). Radial null curves satisfy \(dt/dr=\pm f^{-1}\). Since
\[
 \int_0^{r_0}\frac{dr}{1+2a/r}<\infty,
\]
there are outgoing radial rays from arbitrarily close to the singular boundary reaching a regular exterior in finite coordinate time, and no positive root of \(f\) supplies a horizon. The radial curvature component contains \(f''(r)/2=2a/r^3\), which diverges at zero.
\paragraph{The excluded initial-data hypothesis.} On a static spatial slice, the radial proper distance to zero is
\[
 \int_0^{r_0}\frac{dr}{\sqrt{1+2a/r}}<\infty,
\]
by comparison near zero with a constant times \(r^{1/2}\). Removing the singular center therefore leaves an incomplete initial manifold; adjoining it does not give regular data. This candidate violates the source's complete regular Cauchy-data requirement before genericity is even considered.
\paragraph{Full-scope gap.} The calculation does not disprove vacuum weak cosmic censorship. It explains exactly why an explicit visible vacuum singularity is insufficient for the target, which concerns singularities formed from generic regular isolated-system data. The first missing step is either a stable collapse construction producing visibility from such data or a global exterior estimate excluding it in a stated generic topology. No naked example satisfying those hypotheses is supplied.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked lapse positivity, finite null-coordinate travel and finite radial proper distance; retained the complete-regular-data and genericity exclusions. This is a GPT-6 Astra Ultra self-audit, not independent human verification. Prompt A drafting followed by prompt B scope/dependency/boundary self-audit. Checked lapse positivity, finite null-coordinate travel and finite radial proper distance; retained the complete-regular-data and genericity exclusions. The remaining gap is: Prove or exclude visible singularity formation from complete regular asymptotically flat vacuum data in a specified generic topology. Unresolved status and zero original-target completion are retained.

Coordinator checked the negative-mass lapse integrals and incomplete initial spatial slice, which invalidate the proposed shortcut. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 and local file-reading/writing tools for manuscript serialization and structural checks; mathematical calculations were symbolic reasoning, with no numerical experiment or theorem prover. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
\textbf{UNRESOLVED}. Prove or exclude visible singularity formation from complete regular asymptotically flat vacuum data in a specified generic topology.

